  "prompt": "Until archaeologists actually dug up the bones underneath our feet. Because here is the strange paradox of modern progress: we built washing machines, microwaves, and cars to save us time, yet you drown in paperwork while he relaxed by the fire. At dig sites around the world, scientists measured ancient skeletons, comparing hunter-gatherer bones against the early farmers who came later. And the transition from foraging to farming shocked historians: early farmers were shorter, sicker, and worked twice as hard.",
